1. Requesting Permission

1. Contact: You must contact the copyright holder via Discord at @willow627 (preferred) or by email at Willownokstella@gmail.com, describing how you intend to use the project.
2. Valid Proof of Contact: The 30-day response window only begins if you send a message via one of the exact methods listed above and retain verifiable proof of delivery (such as a timestamped Discord DM or sent email receipt). Messages sent to other platforms, accounts, or public comments do not count.
3. Denial: If the copyright holder explicitly denies your request, you may not use the project.
4. Approval: If the copyright holder explicitly approves your request, you may use the project under the agreed terms.
5. 30-Day Timeout: If the copyright holder does not respond within thirty (30) calendar days of receiving a valid request, permission is automatically granted to use, copy, modify, publish, and sell the project or derivative works, provided you meet all attribution conditions below.

2. Attribution & Ownership Conditions

-Credit: You must give clear, visible credit to **Willow (Will0W-N)** as the original creator in your project description, credits, or repository (e.g., on the Steam Workshop page and in the mod files).
-Steam Workshop Contributor: If you publish this mod or any derivative/continuation of it to the Steam Workshop, you must add the holder as a Contributor (friend code provided on request) on the Steam Workshop page so the original creator can stay connected to the project. *(Note: You may need to send a Steam friend request to add a contributor; if the copyright holder does not accept within 14 days, listing clear text credit in the description satisfies this requirement.)*
-No False Authorship: You may not claim original authorship of the base mod or its assets, even if modified.

